hadiths[19]{hadithnumber,text}:
"171","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): Among the Jews, when a woman would menstruate, they would neither eat with her nor stay with her in the house. The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked him about this, so Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""They ask you about menstruation. Say: It is a harm, so keep away from women during menstruation"" (__QUR_N__). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do everything except intercourse. When this news reached the Jews, they said: This man (i.e., Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him) wants to oppose us in every matter. Upon hearing this, Sayyiduna Usayd bin Hudayr (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Abbad bin Bishr (may Allah be pleased with him) came and said: O Messenger of Allah! The Jews say such and such, so why should we not have intercourse with menstruating women? (Meaning, since the Jews dislike our opposition and are annoyed by it, we should oppose them thoroughly.) Upon hearing this, the color of the Messenger of Allah’s (peace and blessings be upon him) face changed. (He disliked their suggestion to have intercourse because it was against the Qur'an.) We thought that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was angry with these two persons. They got up and left. Meanwhile, someone sent milk as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he called both of them back and gave them milk to drink. Then they realized that his anger was not upon them."
"172","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that (the daughter of Shakl or the daughter of Yazid bin Sakan) Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about the ritual bath (ghusl) after menstruation. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: First, take water with lotus leaves and purify yourself well with it (i.e., wash and clean the menstrual blood that is present), then pour water over your head and rub vigorously so that the water reaches the roots of the hair. Then pour water over yourself (i.e., over the whole body). Then take a piece of cotton or cloth scented with musk and purify yourself with it. Lady Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) asked: How should I purify myself with it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Subhan Allah! Purify yourself with it.” Then Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) quietly said: Apply it to the place of blood. Then she asked about the ritual bath after sexual impurity (janabah), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Take water and purify yourself well, then pour water over your head and rub so that the water reaches all the roots, then pour water over your whole body. Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: How excellent were the women of the Ansar, they did not feel shy to ask about matters of religion. (And this is necessary, because modesty is in sin and disobedience, and asking about religious matters is reward and merit.)"
"173","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the mosque when he said to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): ""Hand me the cloth."" She said, ""I am menstruating."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Your menstruation is not in your hand."" Then she handed him the cloth."
"174","‘A’ishah Siddiqah, Mother of the Believers (may Allah be pleased with her), says: When I was in i‘tikaf, I would go home for a need, and as I walked, if there was anyone sick in the house, I would ask about them. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would stay in the mosque and extend his head towards me, and I would comb his hair. And when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was in i‘tikaf, he would not enter the house except for a need."
"175","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would recline in my lap and recite the Qur’an while I was menstruating."
"176","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I was lying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) under a sheet when suddenly I began menstruating. I slipped away and took my menstrual clothes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Have you started your menses?” I said, “Yes.” He called me, and then I lay with him under the same sheet. The narrator of the hadith (Zaynab) said that Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform ghusl for janabah from the same vessel."
"177","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When any woman among us would menstruate, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would order her to tie a waist-wrapper during the flow of menstrual blood, then he would have intimacy with her (that is, he would lie with his wife). Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Who among you has as much control over his desire and need as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had?"
"178","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I used to drink water, then after drinking I would give the vessel to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he would place his mouth at the same spot where I had placed my mouth and drink the water, even though I was menstruating. And I used to gnaw on a bone, then give it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he would place his mouth at the same spot where I had placed mine."
"179","‘Mother of the Believers Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that Umm Habibah bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her) asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that she was experiencing istihada (non-menstrual bleeding), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “This blood is from a vein, so perform ghusl and pray.” Then she used to perform ghusl for every prayer. Laith said that Ibn Shihab did not state that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered her to perform ghusl for every prayer, rather Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her) did so herself."
"180","Narrated from Sayyida Mu’adhah (may Allah be pleased with her): I asked Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), “What is the reason that a menstruating woman makes up the missed fasts but does not make up the missed prayers?” She replied, “Are you a Haruriyyah?” I said, “No, I am only asking.” She said, “We used to experience menstruation, and we were ordered to make up the fasts, but we were not ordered to make up the prayers.” (What an excellent answer: religion is the name of following the commands of Allah and His Messenger; what was commanded, we did, and what was not commanded, we did not do.)"
"181","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There are five acts of fitrah, or five things are from fitrah: 1. Circumcision. 2. Shaving the pubic hair. 3. Cutting the nails. 4. Plucking the armpit hair. 5. Trimming the moustache."""
"182","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa Tayyiba Tahira (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Ten things are from the natural disposition (fitrah): 1: Trimming the mustache. 2: Letting the beard grow. 3: Using the miswak. 4: Putting water in the nose. 5: Cutting the nails. 6: Washing the finger joints (washing inside the ears, nose, armpits, and thighs). 7: Plucking the armpit hair. 8: Shaving the pubic hair. 9: Cleaning oneself with water after relieving oneself (or sprinkling a little water on the private parts after ablution). Mus’ab said: I forgot the tenth thing; perhaps it is rinsing the mouth. Waki’ (may Allah have mercy on him) said: “Intiqas al-ma’” (which is mentioned in the hadith) means cleaning oneself after relieving oneself."
"183","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that I saw myself using a miswak in a dream. Then two men asked me for the miswak; one of them was older. I gave the miswak to the younger one, so I was instructed to give it to the older one, so I gave it to the older one."
"184","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: (In all words and actions) oppose the polytheists; trim the moustaches and let the beards grow (that is, leave the beards and do not trim them)."
"185","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that a time limit was set for us regarding trimming the moustache, cutting the nails, plucking the armpit hair, and shaving the pubic hair, that they should not be left for more than forty days."
"186","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We were sitting in the mosque with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a Bedouin came and started urinating while standing. The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out to him to stop, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Do not interrupt his urination, leave him."" So the people left him until he finished urinating. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said, ""Mosques are not for urination or filth. They are built for the remembrance of Allah, for prayer, and for reciting the Qur'an,"" or he said something similar. Then he ordered a man, who brought a bucket of water and poured it over the spot."
"187","It is narrated from Umm Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) that she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with her child who did not eat food. Ubaidullah (the narrator of the hadith) said that Umm Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) informed that the child urinated in the lap of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called for water and sprinkled it on the garment and did not wash it."
"188","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Shihab Khawlani narrates that I stayed as a guest with Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her). I had a wet dream in my clothes, so I dipped them in water. The slave girl of Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) saw me and went to inform her. Umm al-Mu’minin sent me a message asking why I had done that. I said that in my sleep I saw what a sleeper sees (i.e., a wet dream). Umm al-Mu’minin asked, “Did you see any trace (of semen) on your clothes?” I said, “No.” She said, “If you had seen anything on your clothes, even then washing that spot would have been sufficient. I used to scrape off the dried semen from the clothes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with my fingernails.”"
"189","Lady Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with both of them) says that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and asked, ""If menstrual blood gets on any of our clothes, what should she do?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""First, she should scrape it off, then pour water over it, rub it, and wash it. After that, she may pray in the same garment."""
